hadiths[59]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2228","Both Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid and Majma bin Yazid, the Ansari brothers, narrated that a man of the Ansar, who was called Khadham, married his daughter whom he did not like. Yahya bin Saeed said: He has heard that this woman was Saiba."
"2229","It was narrated from Abd al-Rahman and Majma, the two sons of Yazid bin Jariyah, that their father married Sayyida Khansa bint Jazam, may God be pleased with her."
"2230","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir or Sayyidna Samra bin Jundab, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A woman who is married to two guardians (one to one person and the other to another person)"," then that woman will be given to the one with whom she was married first"," and if a person sells an item to two men"," it will be given to the one who sold it first.\"""""
"2231","From this chain of transmission, Hasan narrated the same hadith from Sayyidna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) as mentioned above."
"2232","On the authority of Rabi' bin Sabrah, his father (Sayyiduna Subrah, may God be pleased with him) narrated a hadith that he was going with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the farewell Hajj, that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Have pleasure with these women\"""," and pleasure means marriage according to us. We presented this order to some women. They refused to marry us without setting a fixed period. The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings of God be upon him"," said: \""Set a period.\"" (He took a liking to Sabra) and decided between us for ten days. So let him go and do not take back from them what he has given him.”"""
"2233","On the authority of Rabi bin Sabra Jahni, his father said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Nikah Mutah at the time of the conquest of Makkah."
"2234","Sayyidna Ali (RA) said to Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) forbade sexual intercourse with women and eating the meat of domestic donkeys in the year of Khaybar."
"2235","It was narrated from Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Uthman Ibn Affan (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \A man in Ihram (in the state of Ihram) should neither marry himself nor marry anyone else.\"""""
"2236","It is narrated on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, may God have mercy on him, that I asked Sayyida Aisha (RA) that how much was the dowry of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). He said: The dowry of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was twelve Oqiyas and one Nish. He said: No. He said: Half an Oqiya, this was the dowry of the wives of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2237","Abu Ajfa Salmi said: Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, praised Allah and said: Be careful not to exaggerate the dowry of women, because if (excessive dowry) was a cause of honor and honor in the world and piety in the sight of Allah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would have been the first to deserve it (i.e., he kept more of the dowry of wives and daughters), although the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave one of his wives and a girl. The seal is not more than twelve ounces, be careful, listen! One of you abuses and abuses the dowry of his wife until his heart becomes enmity from her and he says: I suffered for you like lifting a rope of musk or I sweat like water of musk."
"2238","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (RA) said: A woman came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said that she gave her life for Allah and the Messenger (this was an allusion to marriage). The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \I do not need women anymore.\"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""You clothe him as a dowry.\"" He said: \""I have no other clothes.\"" He said: \""Give me something even if it is an iron ring.\"" The narrator said: He showed his disability even with this"," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Do you remember anything from the Holy Qur'an?\"" He said: You remember such and such a surah"," he said: \""Go"," I have given it to you in marriage"," in exchange for the Qur'an that you remember.\"""""
"2239","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radi Allahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, taught us this sermon about need and need: Verily, all praise is due to Allah alone, we praise Him and seek His help and seek His forgiveness and forgiveness and seek refuge in Allah from the evil of our souls. Messenger, then recite these three verses: “O you who believe, fear Allah and do not die except while you are Muslims” [Al-Imran: 102/3], O people, fear your Lord, Who created you from a single soul, and created from it its mates, and sent forth from them many men. And women, and fear Allah, Whom you ask, and the Most Merciful. Indeed, Allah has been a rival to you.” [An-Nisa: 1/4] “O you who believe. Fear Allah and say a clear word: He will correct your deeds and forgive you your sins. [Al-Ahzab: 70/33-71], then he would state his need (i.e. after that he would propose and accept the marriage)."
"2240","On the authority of Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \The conditions by which you have made the private parts of women lawful are the most deserving of fulfillment.\"""""
"2241","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) saw a yellowish color (i.e. the color of saffron on the body or clothes) on Sayyidna Abdur Rahman Bin Awf (RA) and said: \What is this yellowness?\"" He said: I have married a woman for a kernel of gold (i.e. for gold equal to a kernel of dates"," which is about three dirhams)."""
"2242","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When one of you is invited to the invitation of Walima"," he should accept this invitation\"" (i.e."," he must go to it). Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He should accept the invitation"," but food is not obligatory for him."""
"2243","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who has two wives and is more inclined towards one"," he will come on the Day of Resurrection with half of his torso bent (as if bent due to paralysis).\"""""
"2244","Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to maintain justice with each wife and among all wives, and would say: \O Allah"," this is my duty in a matter of which I am the owner"," and do not blame me in a matter of which you are the owner and I am not the owner of it.\"""""
"2245","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to travel, he used to cast lots for his wives and take the one whose name was drawn."
"2246","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: \There are seven days for a virgin and three days for a female.\"""""
"2247","It was narrated from Sayyidah Umm Salamah that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, he stayed with her for three days and said: \Your status is not low in my eyes. If you want"," I can stay with you for seven days"," then I will stay with each wife for seven days.\"" (And then your turn will come after everyone"," but they said: Stay with everyone one day at a time and come to me)."""
"2248","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me in Shawwal and kept company with me in Shawwal. And Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) liked that her female relatives should leave in Shawwal."
"2249","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you has sexual intercourse with his wife, what prevents him from making this supplication (i.e., he should make this supplication at the time of sexual intercourse)? Razaqtna» “I begin with the name of Allah, O Allah, save us from Satan and keep Satan away from what You give us (as a result of this intercourse). After reciting this dua, Satan can never harm the offspring that the husband and wife will get from this intercourse."
"2250","Sayyidna Khuzima bin Thabit (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Surely Allah does not shy away from speaking the truth. Do not have intercourse with women in their presence.\"""""
"2251","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) that the Jews said to the Muslims: A man who sleeps behind his wife will have a child with a baby, so Allah revealed this honorable verse: Want it.”"
"2252","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a woman who fell in love with him. He (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) came to Umm al-Mu’minin, Sayyidah Saudah (may Allah be pleased with him), who was distilling perfume and there were women sitting near her. They left the women and went away. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fulfilled his desire. Let him fulfill his desire) because the wife also has the same (for necessities) that this woman has."
"2253","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we returned, I started hurrying. Suddenly, a rider came from behind. You said to me: \Why are you in a hurry?\"" Said: Because I have newly married. He said: \""Which marriage is with a virgin girl or with a married woman?\"" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""The husband is married to a woman. He said: \""Why not with a virgin? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""After reaching home"," companionship is only companionship and meeting.\"" Then when we entered Madinah"," the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \""Stay and wait until the night falls"," that is"," until Isha"," so that the woman with disheveled hair can beautify herself"," and the one whose husband has gone out can clean himself up.\"""""
"2254","Sayyida Jadama bint Wahib Asadiyya (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I intended to forbid sexual intercourse with a lactating woman"," but I remembered that the people of Rome and Persia do so and their children are not harmed.\"" Imam al-Darmi"," may God have mercy on him"," said: \""Gheela\"" means that a woman breastfeeds a child and has sexual intercourse with her."""
"2255","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never killed a servant, nor did he kill anyone else with his hand, but he (peace be upon him) used to wage jihad in the way of Allah."
"2256","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abi Dhubab (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) said: “Do not kill the captives of Allah”, (i.e. the wives) then Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (SAW) and said: (By this order) women have become bold against their husbands (i.e. they are willing to speak tongues and mischief). They gathered to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and began to complain about their husbands, so the Messenger of God, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Many women complain to the wives of Muhammad"," peace and blessings be upon him"," about their husbands. These people (i.e. those who beat their wives) are not good.\"""""
"2257","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zam'ah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon and admonished the people about women."
"2258","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Verily"," a woman was created from a rib"," so if you straighten her"," she will break it"," so treat her with good manners"," because she has crookedness and relief.\"""""
"2259","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \A woman is (crooked) like a rib. If you try to straighten her"," you will break it"," and if you enjoy her with the same crookedness"," you will be benefited.\"""""
"2260","Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: A companion asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) about ``Izl'', and he (PBUH) said: \Do you do that? If you don't do it"," there is no problem"," but the soul that Allah has decreed to be born will certainly continue to be born"," whether you do it or not.\"""""
"2261","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) said: We said: O Messenger of Allah! A man has a concubine, he has intercourse with her and does not want her to conceive, can he divorce her? Such a man has a woman (wife) and she is breastfeeding, the man has intercourse with her and does not want her to become pregnant, in such a case can he divorce his wife? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There is nothing wrong if you do not depose"," it is a matter of destiny.\"" Ibn Aoun said: I narrated this tradition to Hasan"," and he said: By Allah"," in this sentence (\""La alaikum\"")"," there is a warning to refrain from exile"," to refrain from exile."""
"2262","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “There is no one more jealous than Allah, that is why He forbade immorality and immorality, and there is no one who loves His own praise more than Allah.”"
"2263","Ibn Jabir bin Atiq said: My father narrated to me the hadith that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is one type of honor that Allah likes and one type of honor that Allah dislikes, and the type of honor that Allah likes is that a person should show honor in place of doubt (such as if someone laughs at his wife in private, then he becomes jealous), and the honor that Allah does not like is that without doubt (and evidence). He should be jealous for no reason (like if a man leaves his house and kills him out of jealousy without investigation)."
"2264","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) heard that Sayyidna Sa’d Bin ‘Ubada (RA) says: If I see a man with his wife, I will kill him with the sword and never leave him. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Do you wonder at the jealousy of Saad? I am more jealous than him, and Allah Almighty is more jealous than me. And no one is more proud than Allah, and no one likes excuses more than Allah, that is why Allah sent the messengers giving good news and warning (so that the servants may make excuses and repent before punishment) and no one likes praise more than Allah, so Allah promised Paradise (so that the servants will worship and praise Him and attain Paradise)."
"2265","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If a woman spends a night separated from her husband's bed due to her displeasure with him"," the angels will curse her until she desist from this behavior.\"""""
"2266","It was narrated from Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad (RA) that Sayyidna Awaimar Ajlani (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! What do you think if a man finds a non-man with his wife? Should he kill him? In that case people will kill him (in turn), then what should he do? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Allah has revealed about you and your wife. Go and bring your wife with you.\"" Sayyidna Sahl (RA) said: Then both the husband and wife cursed"," and the people were present with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) at that time. If I keep her even after that"," it will mean that I am a liar"," then they divorced her thrice before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything. Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhri"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Then this method of cursing became common for those who cursed."""
"2267","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that Sayyidna Awaymar, may God be pleased with him, came to Sayyidna Asim bin Adi, may God be pleased with him, he was the leader of Banu Ajlan, and he narrated a hadith similar to the above-mentioned hadith, but he did not mention the word \talaqha talasa\"" in it"," that he divorced three times."""
"2268","Abdul Malik bin Abi Sulaiman said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, saying that I was asked about those who cursed in the Emirate during the reign of Musab bin Zubayr: Will they be separated? I wondered what to answer, so I went to the house of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar and said to the slave: Bring me permission to enter. He said: They are resting at that time and you cannot enter. Saeed said: Sayyiduna Ibn Umar heard my voice and said: Is it Ibn Jubayr? I said: Yes, they said: Come, at that time you must have come for something important. I entered and saw that he was sitting on a blanket and leaning on a pillow filled with palm bark. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman! Will there be separation among those who curse? Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, said: Glory be to God, surely there will be a separation, and so-and-so bin so-and-so was the first to ask about it, and he said: O Messenger of God! May Allah's blessings be upon you, tell me what would a man do if he sees his wife committing adultery? If he remains silent, how can he remain silent on such a big matter and if he utters such a thing from his mouth, he will utter bad words. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent and did not answer him, then he got up due to some need of his own, then (one day) that person appeared in the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said that he himself was afflicted with what I had asked him about, then Allah revealed these verses of Surah Noor:"
"2269","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) separated the cursing husband and wife and gave the child to its mother."
"2270","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A slave who marries without the permission of his master is an adulterer.\"""""
"2271","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A slave who marries without the permission of his master is an adulterer.\"""""
"2272","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The child belongs to the one in whose bed it is born"," and a stone is for the adulterer.\"""""
"2273","It was narrated from Sayyida Aisha, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The child (sahib) belongs to the mattress.\"""""
"2274","Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyida Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Utbah bin Abi Waqqas (when he died) had bequeathed to his brother Sayyidna Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the son of the concubine of Zam'ah is mine and that he should take him into his custody. He took the boy who was more similar to Utbah bin Abi Waqqas among the people. When this case came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he gave a decision: \This child"," O Abd bin Zam'ah"," is for you"," because he was born on his father's bed.\"" (Because at that time the child's mother was in the possession of Abd bin Zam'ah)"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wife"," Umm al-Mu'minin"," Sayyidah Saudah bint Zamahh"," may God be pleased with her: \""O Saudah! Cover this boy\"""," he said this because of the resemblance that the boy bore to Utbah bin Abi Waqqas."""
"2275","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, when the verse of Cursing was revealed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he was saying: “A woman who introduces a lineage into a nation that is not of them (i.e. a woman gives birth to a child by adultery and ascribes it to her husband as his offspring), that woman is nothing in the sight of Allah, and Allah will never admit such a woman to Paradise, and a man who, knowing his offspring, If he refuses (i.e. knowingly and knowingly calls his child a forbidden child), he will not be blessed with the sight of Allah (on the Day of Resurrection), and Allah will humiliate him in front of all the people before and after him. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Muhammad bin Ka'b al-Qarzi narrated and Saeed narrated this hadith and said: I received this hadith from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2276","Yazid bin Bara narrated from his father, he said: I met my uncle who was with Jhandi, I said: Where are you going? He said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, has sent me to a man who has married his father's wife, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, has ordered me to behead him and take away his property."
"2277","A man of the Ansar whose name was Ziyad said: I asked Sayyiduna Abi Ka'b (RA): What do you think if all the wives of the Prophet (PBUH) died, would it be permissible for him (PBUH) to marry? He said: Yes, because Allah Ta'ala has made the gender of women permissible in this verse \(﴿"""
"2278","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Before the death of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Allah made it lawful for you to marry any woman you want."
"2279","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Safiyyah bint Hayy (may God be pleased with him) and declared her freedom as a seal."
"2280","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, first freed Umm al-Mominin Sayyida Safiyyah, then married her and declared her freedom as her dowry."
"2281","Saleh bin Saleh bin Hayy Hamdani said: I was with Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, and a Khorasani man came to his service and said: O Abu Amr! Here, the people of Khorasan say that a man who frees his concubine and then marries her is like a man riding his camel. Imam Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, said that Abu Burda bin Abu Musa narrated to me the hadith that his father said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There are three men who will be given a double (double) reward. One is the man who is from the people of the Book and believed in his Prophet"," then he found the Holy Prophet"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," then he also believed in him and followed him"," and the other is the slave who also did justice to God.\"" And his owners also have a double reward for him. Thirdly"," the man who has a slave girl"," he fed her the best food and taught her the best manners"," then freed her and married her"," there is also a double reward for him. Then Imam Shaabi (may Allah have mercy on him) said to Salih: Remember this hadith which we have narrated to you free of charge"," otherwise people used to go to Medina to hear such hadith. Hashim said: I heard about this hadith in Basra"," so I went to him and asked him about this hadith."""
"2282","Abu Barda has narrated a similar hadith from his father and he from the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"2283","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a man who married a woman but did not fix her dowry and did not keep company with her and died. About this he said: For her, the dowry will be like Nisa and she will have to perform the Idda and she will also get a share in the inheritance. Sayyiduna Muaqal Ashjaji (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also made a similar decision about a woman from Burua bint Washiq bin Nawarwas as you have said. Sayyiduna Ibn Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) was happy to hear this. Muhammad and Sufyan said: Ours is also the same creed."
"2284","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: She was with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) in the house of Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) when she heard a man's voice and said: O Messenger! I heard a man enter your house? The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \I think he will be such and such a man.\"" He was the foster uncle of Sayyida Hafsa. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! If my uncle was alive"," could he come to my house? The Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: \""Yes"," breastfeeding proves the same sanctity as birth.\"""""
"2285","Sayyida Aisha reported that her (foster) uncle Abu Qais' brother (Afalah) came to her after the Hijab order, seeking permission to enter. Sayyida Aisha (RA) refused permission and said to seek permission from the Messenger of Allah (SAW), then when the Messenger of Allah (SAW) came, Sayyida Aisha (RA) mentioned it to him and said, \The brother of my foster uncle Abu Qais came (and asked permission to enter)"," so I turned him back until I asked him?\"" He (peace be upon him) said: \""Isn't he your foster uncle?\"" He said: I was breastfed by a woman and not by a man (then how was the sanctity of a man i.e. Abu Qais or his brother proved?) He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""He (Afalah) is your uncle"," he can come in to you.\"" Urwa said: And Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to say: What is forbidden by birth is also forbidden by breastfeeding."""
"2286","Umm al-Mu'minin narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Those (relationships) that are forbidden by birth are also forbidden by adoption."
